Offline mode had three critical failures: new records (clients/employees/tasks) weren't persisted, QR clock-in/out showed error messages despite succeeding, and unvisited routes displayed Chrome's network error page.

## Changes

### New record persistence
**Root cause**: Add dialogs early-returned when offline without calling Firestore operations, despite offline persistence being enabled.

```typescript
// Before: returned early, data lost
if (!isOnline) {
  toast({ title: 'Client Added', ... });
  return; // ❌ Never calls addDoc
}
await addDoc(collection, data);

// After: let Firestore handle offline queueing
await addDoc(collection, data);
toast({
  description: addOfflineIndicator(message, isOnline) // Shows "(Saved locally...)" when offline
});
```

**Files**: `clients/add-client-dialog.tsx`, `employees/add-employee-dialog.tsx`, `tasks/add-task-dialog.tsx`

### Error handling
**Root cause**: Permission errors emitted for all caught exceptions, including successful offline operations that would sync later.

```typescript
} catch (serverError) {
  // Before: always emitted, triggered error boundary
  errorEmitter.emit('permission-error', permissionError);

  // After: only emit when online (actual permission errors)
  if (isOnline) {
    errorEmitter.emit('permission-error', permissionError);
  } else {
    toast({ variant: 'destructive', ... }); // User-friendly message
  }
}
```

**Files**: `time-tracking/page.tsx` (clock-in/out functions), add dialogs

### Offline fallback page
Created `/offline` route served by service worker when navigating to uncached pages offline. Auto-redirects on reconnection.

**Config**: Enhanced `next.config.ts` with NetworkFirst caching strategies for pages and googleapis.com API calls. Fixed regex security issue (unescaped wildcard).

### Automatic page pre-caching
**New feature**: Eliminates the need to manually visit all pages before going offline.

Created `PagePrecacher` component that automatically pre-caches all important pages (dashboard, clients, employees, tasks, time-tracking, payroll, invoicing) in the background after login. Pre-caching starts 1 second after authentication to avoid blocking initial render.

```typescript
// Pages are automatically fetched and cached by service worker
const pagesToCache = [
  '/dashboard', '/clients', '/employees', '/tasks',
  '/time-tracking', '/payroll', '/invoicing'
];
```

**Files**: `components/page-precacher.tsx`, `app/(app)/layout.tsx`

**Benefits**: 
- No manual navigation required to cache pages
- All pages available offline from first login
- Seamless offline experience without preparation

## Testing
See `OFFLINE_MODE_FIXES_TESTING.md` for test procedures. Spanish documentation in `CORRECCIONES_MODO_OFFLINE_ES.md`.

**Testing auto pre-cache**: Login and wait 2-3 seconds. Check browser console for "Pre-cached: /dashboard" messages. Go offline and navigate to any page—all should load successfully without prior visits.

